<LegalLayout title="Frequently Asked Questions" description="Answers to common questions about Water Heater Boys service, scheduling, warranties, service areas, and water-heater options.">
<article><p class="eyebrow">COMMON QUESTIONS</p><h1>Frequently asked questions</h1><p class="legal-date">Straight answers before you schedule.</p>
<h2>How soon can you install a new water heater?</h2><p>Same-day and next-day service is typically available, depending on your location, scheduling, equipment availability, and the work required. Call us at <a href="tel:6508442305">650-844-2305</a> to discuss the situation.</p>
<h2>Do you install tankless and heat-pump water heaters?</h2><p>Yes. We install traditional gas tank, gas tankless, and hybrid heat-pump water heaters. We can discuss your existing setup, household needs, installation space, and available utilities before recommending an option.</p>
<h2>Are you licensed and insured?</h2><p>Yes. Water Heater Boys is a licensed and insured California plumbing contractor. Our California license number is 1134458.</p>
<h2>What areas do you serve?</h2><p>We serve San Francisco, the Peninsula, the East Bay, and the South Bay through San Jose. We do not serve the North Bay. Visit our <a href="/service-areas/">service-area page</a> or call to confirm availability for your address.</p>
<h2>Do you install water and seismic gas shut-off valves?</h2><p>Yes. We install smart water shut-off systems and seismic gas shut-off valves. Requirements vary by property and insurer, so confirm any insurance-specific requirements directly with your carrier.</p>
<h2>Does your work include a warranty?</h2><p>Our work is backed by a one-year workmanship warranty. Equipment may also include a separate manufacturer warranty with its own terms. Your written estimate and service documents describe the warranty that applies to your job.</p>
<h2>Can you estimate the work using photos?</h2><p>Often, yes. For many straightforward projects, we can gather useful information by phone and text, including photographs of the equipment and surrounding connections. Some projects still require an in-person evaluation before the scope and price can be finalized.</p>
<p class="legal-callout">Have another question? <a href="/#estimate">Send us a service request</a> or call <a href="tel:6508442305">650-844-2305</a>.</p></article>
</LegalLayout>
